note the names the fn line mem[p, q) declares: the function, then each parameter
fn nmsig p ulong q ulong to void
a = skipsp add p 3 q
w = wordend a q
nmadd a sub w a
a = skipsp w q
while lt a q bound 9223372036854775807
w = wordend a q
if meq a w twto
ret
end
nmadd a sub w a
a = skipsp w q
w = wordend a q
if or meq a w twview meq a w twedit
a = skipsp w q
w = wordend a q
a = skipsp w q
w = wordend a q
end
a = skipsp w q
end
end

note the names the body line mem[p, q) declares: `NAME = ..` and `for NAME ..`
fn nmline p ulong q ulong to void
a = skipsp p q
w = wordend a q
b = skipsp w q
x = wordend b q
if ge b q
ret
end
if meq a w twfor
nmadd b sub x b
ret
end
if meq b x tweq
nmadd a sub w a
end
end

note the line mem[p, q) in normal form onto nrm: words joined by one space, declared names as
note v and their index, a newline; blank and note lines add nothing
fn nline p ulong q ulong to void
